I come back to my room.
I have a box of sweets in my hand.
I put that box on a small table.
After that, I open my laptop.
I make a video call to my family.
Now it is Sunday morning in Kochi.
But in Mexico, it is Saturday night.
The screen lights up on the laptop.
I see my mother and father.
They are in their living room.
There is a big smile on their faces.
Mother asks, "Maya, are you well?"
I smile and say, "I am fine, Amma."
Father asks, "Is your new room nice?"
I say, "Yes Acha, it is a nice room."
Then I ask them, "Who else is at home now?"
Mother says, "Your older brother and younger sister are here."
I am very happy.
